// endpoint_list_slack_channels.proto — ListSlackChannels: every Slack channel
// the user is a member of on their work Slack, for the host-native composer to
// complete as the user types `#`. HOST section, beside ListSlashCommands.
//
// THE LIST IS THE USER'S, NOT A WORKSPACE'S. Channel membership belongs to the
// person at the keyboard, so the request names no workspace and every composer
// of the daemon is answered the same list.
//
// THE DAEMON READS IT THROUGH GNS, ON DEMAND. The daemon asks the work
// account's Slack (`gns slack channel list-mine`) the first time any composer
// asks, keeps the answer, and reads it again once it is an hour old. A read
// takes seconds, so an ask is never held on one: it is answered from what is
// in hand, and the read it started lands for the next ask. One read runs at a
// time however many composers ask.
